  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that Loperamide oxide may exert its biological effects on the Ca9-22 cell line through multiple indirect pathways. The drug is implicated in the target UDP-glucuronosyltransferase 1-3, which is a key enzyme in the glucuronidation of various compounds. This enzyme is targeted by two distinct molecules: (1R,2R,5R,8S,11S,12R)-12-methyl-6-methylidene-14-oxapentacyclo[10.3.3.15,8.01,11.02,8]nonadecan-13-one and methyl cis-icos-11-enoate, both of which are themselves targets of the Ca9-22 cell line. Additionally, Nimustine, another compound that is targeted by UDP-glucuronosyltransferase 1-3, also shows a relationship with the Ca9-22 cell line. These findings collectively indicate that Loperamide oxide may influence the Ca9-22 cell line via the UDP-glucuronosyltransferase 1-3 pathway, potentially through the action of multiple substrates that are themselves targets of the cell line. The evidence supports a mechanistic link between Loperamide oxide and the Ca9-22 cell line, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated."
